IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `written-law-interface`
IMPORT `pca-types`

-- Prevention of Corruption Act 1960: the officers (ss 3, 4), the powers of arrest and investigation (Part 4: ss 15 to 22) and the
-- procedural sections of Part 6 (ss 32 to 35, 37).
-- Source: source/PCA1960.txt lines 174 to 220 (ss 3, 4), 696 to 915 (Part 4), 1033 to 1074 and 1097 to 1108 (ss 32 to 35, 37).
--
-- The question this module answers: WHO MAY DO WHAT TO WHOM, AND HOW IS THE CASE BROUGHT?  The Act gives the Director of the Corrupt
-- Practices Investigation Bureau and its special investigators police powers for these offences (and a few others), makes every offence under
-- the Act arrestable for the Criminal Procedure Code 2010, requires the Public Prosecutor's consent to prosecute, and gives a District Court
-- the full punishment.  The answers the Code needs (arrestable; the District Court) are packaged in
-- `the Prevention of Corruption Act 1960's statement about its offences`, a record declared in written-law-interface.l4.

§ `3 and 4. The officers`

-- 3(3): the Director's powers may be exercised by a deputy director or an assistant director, subject to the Director's orders and directions.
-- 3(4): a deputy director and an assistant director may exercise the powers conferred by the Act on a special investigator.  The Act
-- usually names "the Director or any special investigator", so those two and the deputy and assistant directors are the officers who may
-- act (fork F4 in NOTES.md: the deputy and assistant director act through 3(3) and (4), not by the section's own words).
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 3(3) and (4)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may exercise the powers conferred by the Act on the Director or a special investigator` IF
        r EQUALS `the Director of the Corrupt Practices Investigation Bureau`
    OR  r EQUALS `a deputy director`
    OR  r EQUALS `an assistant director`
    OR  r EQUALS `a special investigator`

-- 4(1): the Director, deputy directors, assistant directors and special investigators "shall be deemed to be public servants within the meaning of
-- the Penal Code 1871" (the Code's own definition of "public servant" is in sg/penal-code-1871).  4(2): a warrant card is evidence of appointment.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 4(1)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is deemed a public servant within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871` IF
    `the officer may exercise the powers conferred by the Act on the Director or a special investigator` r

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 17(2), 258(2) and 20(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 as read by s 17(2)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is deemed to be an officer not below the rank of inspector of police` IF
        r EQUALS `the Director of the Corrupt Practices Investigation Bureau`
    OR  r EQUALS `a special investigator`

-- Used by the search and warrant rules below.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 22(1) and (2)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is a special investigator or a police officer not below the rank of inspector` IF
        r EQUALS `a special investigator`
    OR  r EQUALS `a police officer of or above the rank of assistant superintendent`
    OR  r EQUALS `a police officer not below the rank of inspector but below assistant superintendent`

-- Any police officer, of any rank.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 16(1)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is a police officer` IF
        r EQUALS `a police officer of or above the rank of assistant superintendent`
    OR  r EQUALS `a police officer not below the rank of inspector but below assistant superintendent`
    OR  r EQUALS `another police officer`

§ `15. Powers of arrest`

-- 15(1): the Director or any special investigator may without a warrant arrest any person who "has been concerned in any offence under this
-- Act or against whom a reasonable complaint has been made or credible information has been received or a reasonable suspicion exists of his
-- having been so concerned".  Any one of the four grounds is enough.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 15(1)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, a IS AN `Arrest Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may arrest the person without a warrant` IF
        `the officer may exercise the powers conferred by the Act on the Director or a special investigator` r
    AND (   a's `the person has been concerned in an offence under this Act`
         OR a's `a reasonable complaint has been made against the person of having been so concerned`
         OR a's `credible information has been received that the person was so concerned`
         OR a's `a reasonable suspicion exists of the person's having been so concerned`)

-- 15(2): the arresting Director or special investigator may search the person and take possession of all articles found upon him which
-- there is reason to believe were the fruits or other evidence of the crime, "provided that no female shall be searched except by a female".
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 15(2)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, a IS AN `Arrest Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may search the person arrested` IF
        `the officer may arrest the person without a warrant` r a
    AND (   NOT a's `the person arrested is a female`
         OR a's `the searcher is a female`)

-- 15(3): every person so arrested "shall be taken to the Corrupt Practices Investigation Bureau or to a police station".
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 15(3)"
GIVEN `the place is the Corrupt Practices Investigation Bureau` IS A BOOLEAN, `the place is a police station` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the arrested person has been taken to a place section 15(3) allows` IF
        `the place is the Corrupt Practices Investigation Bureau`
    OR  `the place is a police station`

§ `16. Provisions as to bail or bond`

-- 16(1): a person arrested by the Director or any special investigator may be released on bail or on his own bond granted by the Director or any
-- special investigator or any police officer.  16(2): Division 5 of Part 6 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 applies, with references to
-- "officer", "police officer" and "police officer not below the rank of sergeant" read to include the Director or a special investigator, and the
-- reference to the Commissioner of Police in section 92 read to include the Director.  (The Code's rules on bail are not encoded here.)
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 16(1)"
GIVEN `the person was arrested by the Director or a special investigator` IS A BOOLEAN, grantor IS AN `Officer Role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be released on bail or on his or her own bond granted by the grantor` IF
        `the person was arrested by the Director or a special investigator`
    AND (   grantor EQUALS `the Director of the Corrupt Practices Investigation Bureau`
         OR grantor EQUALS `a special investigator`
         OR `the officer is a police officer` grantor)

§ `17, 18, 19, 20, 21. Investigation`

-- 17(1): in any case relating to (a) an offence under section 165 or sections 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871 or a conspiracy, attempt or
-- abetment of one, (b) an offence under this Act, or (c) any arrestable offence under any written law "which may be disclosed in the course of
-- an investigation under this Act", the Director or a special investigator may, "without the order of the Public Prosecutor", exercise all or any
-- of the powers in relation to police investigations given by the Criminal Procedure Code 2010.  Sections 161 to 164 of the Penal Code are NOT
-- in 17(1)(a): for them the Public Prosecutor's order under section 19 is needed.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 17(1)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, i IS AN `Investigation Power Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may exercise police investigation powers without the order of the Public Prosecutor` IF
        `the officer may exercise the powers conferred by the Act on the Director or a special investigator` r
    AND (   i's `the case relates to an offence under section 165 or sections 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or to a conspiracy, attempt or abetment of one`
         OR i's `the case relates to an offence under this Act`
         OR i's `the case relates to an arrestable offence under a written law which may be disclosed in the course of an investigation under this Act`)

-- 19: the Public Prosecutor may by order authorise the Director or a special investigator to exercise, in the case of any offence under any
-- written law, all or any of the powers in relation to police investigations given by the Code.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 19"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, i IS AN `Investigation Power Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may exercise police investigation powers on the order of the Public Prosecutor` IF
        i's `the Public Prosecutor has ordered the investigation`
    AND (   r EQUALS `the Director of the Corrupt Practices Investigation Bureau`
         OR r EQUALS `a special investigator`)

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 17(1) and 19"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, i IS AN `Investigation Power Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may exercise police investigation powers` IF
        `the officer may exercise police investigation powers without the order of the Public Prosecutor` r i
    OR  `the officer may exercise police investigation powers on the order of the Public Prosecutor` r i

-- 18(1): the Public Prosecutor, "if satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that an offence under this Act has been
-- committed", may by order authorise the Director, a police officer of or above the rank of assistant superintendent named in the order, or a
-- special investigator so named, to investigate in the manner specified, including any bank, share, purchase or expense account or any safe
-- deposit box.  The order is "sufficient authority" for the disclosure or production by any person of what the officer requires; failing to
-- is the offence in 18(2) (pca-offences.l4).
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 18(1)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, i IS AN `Investigation Power Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Public Prosecutor's order under section 18(1) may name the officer` IF
        i's `the Public Prosecutor is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that an offence under this Act has been committed`
    AND (   r EQUALS `the Director of the Corrupt Practices Investigation Bureau`
         OR r EQUALS `a special investigator`
         OR r EQUALS `a police officer of or above the rank of assistant superintendent`)

-- 20(1): the Public Prosecutor may, if he considers that evidence of an offence under the Act or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of
-- the Penal Code (or a conspiracy, attempt or abetment) by a person in the service of the Government, a department or a public body is likely
-- to be found in a banker's book relating to that person, his wife or child, or a person reasonably believed to be a trustee or agent for him,
-- by order authorise the Director, a special investigator named, or a police officer of or above the rank of assistant superintendent so named,
-- to inspect the book and take copies of any relevant entry.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 20(1)"
GIVEN r IS AN `Officer Role`, i IS AN `Investigation Power Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Public Prosecutor's order under section 20(1) may authorise the officer to inspect the banker's book` IF
        i's `the Public Prosecutor considers that evidence of an offence under this Act or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or of a conspiracy, attempt or abetment of one, by a person in the service of the Government or of a department or of a public body is likely to be found in a banker's book`
    AND i's `the banker's book relates to that person, to his wife or child, or to a person reasonably believed by the Public Prosecutor to be a trustee or agent for that person`
    AND (   r EQUALS `the Director of the Corrupt Practices Investigation Bureau`
         OR r EQUALS `a special investigator`
         OR r EQUALS `a police officer of or above the rank of assistant superintendent`)

-- 21(1) lists six things the Public Prosecutor may require by written notice (a sworn statement of the person's and his family's property and
-- when each was acquired; a sworn statement of money or property sent out of Singapore; a sworn statement of any other person's property where
-- there are reasonable grounds to believe it can assist; the Comptroller of Income Tax's information; documents of a department or public body;
-- copies of bank accounts).  Their conditions are the same threshold, read in `an offence under section 21(2) is made out` (pca-offences.l4);
-- the six kinds are not enumerated as a type because no rule here depends on which was asked for.

§ `22. Powers of search and seizure`

-- 22(1): where it appears to a Magistrate or to the Director upon information and after such inquiry as he thinks necessary that there is
-- reasonable cause to believe that in a place there is a document containing evidence of, or an article or property relating to, an offence
-- under the Act or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code (or a conspiracy, attempt or abetment), the Magistrate or the
-- Director may by warrant empower a special investigator or police officer not below the rank of inspector to enter by force if necessary and to
-- search, seize and detain.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 22(1)"
GIVEN issuer IS AN `Officer Role`, s IS A `Search Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the issuer may issue a search warrant` IF
        s's `it appears upon information and after such inquiry as the Magistrate or the Director thinks necessary that there is reasonable cause to believe that in a place there is a document containing evidence of, or an article or property relating to, an offence under this Act, or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or a conspiracy, attempt or abetment of one`
    AND (   issuer EQUALS `a Magistrate`
         OR issuer EQUALS `the Director of the Corrupt Practices Investigation Bureau`)

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 22(1)"
GIVEN searcher IS AN `Officer Role`, s IS A `Search Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may enter and search under a warrant` IF
        s's `a warrant has been issued by a Magistrate or the Director, directed to the searcher`
    AND `the officer is a special investigator or a police officer not below the rank of inspector` searcher

-- 22(2): without a warrant, a special investigator or a police officer not below the rank of inspector may exercise the same powers where there
-- is reasonable cause to believe a document, article or property is concealed or deposited in the place AND reasonable grounds for believing
-- that "by reason of the delay in obtaining a search warrant the object of the search is likely to be frustrated".
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 22(2)"
GIVEN searcher IS AN `Officer Role`, s IS A `Search Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may enter and search without a warrant` IF
        `the officer is a special investigator or a police officer not below the rank of inspector` searcher
    AND s's `the special investigator or police officer has reasonable cause to believe that such a document, article or property is concealed or deposited in the place`
    AND s's `the special investigator or police officer has reasonable grounds for believing that by reason of the delay in obtaining a search warrant the object of the search is likely to be frustrated`

§ `32 to 35 and 37. Bringing the case`

-- 32(1): "Every offence under this Act shall be deemed to be an arrestable offence for the purposes of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010."
-- 34: "Notwithstanding the provisions of any written law to the contrary, a District Court shall have jurisdiction to try any offence under this
-- Act and to award the full punishment for that offence."  Neither depends on the offence, so the record is a constant.  The Act says
-- nothing about a Magistrate's Court, and the record says FALSE for it (the Code's own ss 7 to 9 then decide).  The Act's own power of arrest
-- (15(1)) is given to the Director and special investigators and not to the police, so `the Act empowers the police` is FALSE; the police
-- power comes from the Code's rules on an arrestable offence, which 32(1) triggers.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 32(1) and 34"
GIVETH A `Written Law Procedure Statement`
`the Prevention of Corruption Act 1960's statement about its offences` MEANS
    `Written Law Procedure Statement` WITH
        `the Act` IS "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960"
        `the Act deems the offence to be an arrestable offence for the purposes of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` IS TRUE
        `the Act empowers the police to arrest without warrant for the offence` IS FALSE
        `the Act shows the offence as triable by a District Court under that Act` IS TRUE
        `the Act shows the offence as triable by a Magistrate's Court under that Act` IS FALSE

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 32(1)"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every offence under the Act is deemed an arrestable offence` IF
    (`the Prevention of Corruption Act 1960's statement about its offences`)'s `the Act deems the offence to be an arrestable offence for the purposes of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 34"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a District Court may try any offence under the Act and award the full punishment for it` IF
    (`the Prevention of Corruption Act 1960's statement about its offences`)'s `the Act shows the offence as triable by a District Court under that Act`

-- 33: "A prosecution under this Act shall not be instituted except by or with the consent of the Public Prosecutor."
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 33"
GIVEN p IS A `Procedure Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prosecution under the Act may be instituted` IF
        p's `the prosecution is instituted by the Public Prosecutor`
    OR  p's `the prosecution is instituted with the consent of the Public Prosecutor`

-- 35(1): whenever 2 or more persons are charged with an offence under the Act or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code (or
-- a conspiracy, attempt or abetment), the court may require one or more of them to give evidence as a witness for the prosecution.  35(2): one
-- who refuses to be sworn or to answer a lawful question is dealt with as a witness so refusing may be by a Magistrate's Court or District
-- Court.  35(3): every person so required who "in the opinion of the court makes true and full discovery of all things as to which he is
-- lawfully examined" is entitled to a certificate of indemnity, "a bar to all legal proceedings against him in respect of all those things".
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 35(1)"
GIVEN p IS A `Procedure Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may require one or more of the persons charged to give evidence for the prosecution` IF
    p's `two or more persons are charged with an offence under this Act or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or with a conspiracy, attempt or abetment of one`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 35(3)"
GIVEN p IS A `Procedure Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is entitled to a certificate of indemnity` IF
        p's `the person was required by the court under section 35(1) to give evidence as a witness for the prosecution`
    AND p's `the person required to give evidence in the opinion of the court makes true and full discovery of all things as to which he or she is lawfully examined`

-- 37(1): the Act has effect, in relation to citizens of Singapore, outside as well as within Singapore; a citizen who commits an offence under it
-- outside Singapore "may be dealt with in respect of that offence as if it had been committed within Singapore".  37(2): proceedings that would be
-- a bar to later proceedings for the same offence if committed in Singapore are a bar to extradition proceedings for it.
@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 37(1)"
GIVEN p IS A `Procedure Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be dealt with as if the offence had been committed within Singapore` IF
        p's `the accused is a citizen of Singapore`
    AND p's `the offence under this Act was committed in a place outside Singapore`
